e.\n\nThe best play here is to *fold*. I can’t go all in and lose.\n\n\n", 'output': 'Evaluation: The user holds Pocket Sevens (7h, 7s), a medium strength starting hand. The opponent has made a massive overbet (effectively an All-in) of nearly 100 big blinds pre-flop. While 77 is ahead of random hands, it performs poorly against a typical "shoving range" which includes higher pairs (88+) and strong overcards (AK, AQ). Against higher pairs, 77 is a roughly 20% underdog. Against overcards, it is merely a coin flip (~50-52%). Calling an All-in for your entire stack with only a coin-flip or worse probability is generally a negative Expected Value play in this specific deep-stack scenario.\n\nReason: Facing a 100BB shove, the opponent\'s range is likely strong (TT+, AK). Pocket 7s does not have sufficient equity to justify calling off the entire stack, as you are likely either crushed by a higher pair or flipping against overcards. It is better to preserve the stack for a more advantageous spot.\n\nAnswer: -1'}
